tive":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $338K ranks in the bottom quartile among Communication Services peers, improving at 18%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $20K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Gray Media, Inc. is a small-cap communication services business with a $507M market cap on $3.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years and +18% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $181M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 8.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 7.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 53/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Communication Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Communication Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Communication Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Communication Services ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Gray Media (GTN) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/gray-media-gtn-q3-2026-205137000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793999017.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Gray Media (NYSE:GTN) Shares Gap Down Following Weak Earnings","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/gray-media-nysegtn-shares-gap-down-following-weak-earnings.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793978484.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.751,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Gray Television (NYSE:GTN) posts better-than-expected sales in Q3 2026, full-year sales guidance is optimistic","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/gray-television-nyse-gtn-posts-113123670.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793964683.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.866,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"